{ia12}{offset110}{arial}
Reception: {arialbld}Chief Kodbar{arial}

from: Alex Kolman

to: {name}








{offset0}Our men have paid a heavy tribute on the altar of freedom, so that the tulips of Flatland flower again to the turning of the sails of windmills, not to the blades of Psycho bombers.{pause}

Good news from Kurt Rorscham, his 3rd Schyzo army crossed the Zar, continuing his lightning progression eastwards, he liberated Littlestonia in three days. The Tektons now have: Kurt in the south, T-Rex in the south-west and myself "the old man" in the west.{pause}

Our worries {rank} are in the north...{pause}

We know that Psycho scientists established a {arialbld}heavy water{arial} plant in Viklund using electricity from the powerful hydroelectric dam of {arialbld}Telemark.{arial} You could interrogate me on raising tulips but don't ask me anything {name} on the subject of heavy water(1). All I know is that if the Psychos need it, it is bad for us!{pause}

If their mad scientists have not yet been able to achieve their ultimate weapon it's thanks to one man in particular.{pause}

{ia15}{offset105}His name is {arialbld}Markus Boggus,{arial} a former vessel commander in the regular Viklundish navy. He refused the surrender of his country and decided to raise the Jolly Roger on the mast of his battle cruiser, the Graf-Spitz. We owe him 42 acts of piracy against Tekton convoys in the Baltik Sea. Thanks to him and his men's exceptional courage, no delivery of heavy water has yet been able to reach Tektonia.{pause}



{offset0}No point in telling you the Psychos are after him.{pause}
Until now, he could escape from them by finding refuge in the labyrinth of the Viklundish fjords.

Unfortunately we have received a report showing that the Tektons have discovered his hideaway on the {arialbld}Maribo{arial} island.{pause}

We need an exceptional commander to give this Markus Boggus a hand...

The identity of this commander seems obvious to everyone, from the Strategic High Command to the Prime Minister, you will leave within the hour for {arialbld}Borkum{arial}.



{offset150}{arialbld}Alex Kolman{arial}




{offset200}{signature1}{offset0}{pause}{pause}




(1)Heavy water:{micro}

There are two natural isotopes of hydrogen: deuterium and tritium. Normal water consists of two hydrogen atoms for one oxygen atom (H2O), heavy water consists of two deuterium atoms per oxygen atom (D2O). Heavy water is not toxic, it's present in water's natural state (about 0.02 out of 100 by volume), and can be extracted by electrolysis. Given its very low recurrence, a large quantity of water and electricity is needed for extracting a single drop of heavy water. Its density is 1.11 higher than normal water, hence its name "heavy water".

by: Seargent Chief Kodbar, at your service {rank}, I obtained a chemistry degree at Camford.
{}

